<title>UK: German inland gas oil eases, buying still weak.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil eases, buying still weak.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.6807)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     32.10/32.50     19.10/19.34   32.20/32.60</p>
<p> BREMEN		32.10/32.50     19.10/19.34   32.20/32.60</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    32.30/32.70     19.22/19.46   32.40/32.80</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   32.50/32.90     19.34/19.58   32.60/33.00</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   32.40/32.80     19.27/19.52   32.50/32.90</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  33.20/33.70     19.75/20.05   33.30/33.80</p>
<p>German inland gas oil slipped a touch on Friday, but the lower prices failed to attract significantly extra demand.</p>
<p>&quot;Everyone wants lower, lower prices,&quot; commented one trader.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8980</p>
</text>
